      104  ==Economy==
      105  A total of about 15,300 people are employed in the district's businesses. [[Agriculture]] is the main economic sector, covering 81.8% of the total land area. The principal crops include [[cereal]]s ([[wheat]], [[barley]], [[oat]]s), industrial crops such as [[Common sunflower|sunflower]], [[tobacco]
      106  ==Education==
      107  In the district, 35 primary and secondary educational institutions are operating, including 2 [[Primary school|elementary school]]s, 24 [[Gymnasium (school)|gymnasium]]s, and 9 [[lyceum]]s. {{cite web | url= https://fism.gov.md/sites/default/files/document/attachments/hse_riscani.pdf | title=An over
